tags: hibernated-grace, suspended_grace

A promise of the node: how long it keeps a hibernated instance that cannot pay, before
it stops the instance and deletes its state.

The value is seconds, in base 10. Example: 604800 (7 days). A deposit in this time can
wake the instance.

With no promise, the node can stop the instance at once. The node is bound.

=== formal
class=promise
name=hibernated-grace
rule=the node keeps the state of a hibernated instance that cannot pay for at least value seconds before it stops the instance
value=seconds, base 10
